From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] asap7/coralnpu-regfiles-exmem: the floating-point register
 file, generated
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FRegfile keeps its 32 words as separate registers, each split into
mantissa, exponent and sign, beside a scoreboard. surgery.py --fregfile
moves the words into FRegfile_rf: 32 x 32, four combinational reads
(the three read ports and the bus port), two writes of which write port
0 wins a word both write, every word reset to zero while reset is high.
FRegfile keeps the read ports' valid gating, the bus port's bypass of
write port 0 and the scoreboard as they were. The script checks every
register, word decode, write, reset, word select and read against the
shape firtool wrote and stops on anything else.

coralnpu-regfiles-exmem is coralnpu-regfile-exmem with both register
files generated. A simulation of FRegfile against the surgered FRegfile
and FRegfile_rf, 20,000 random cycles with resets and colliding writes,
finds no difference; with the write priority reversed it finds 6,339.

Not upstreamed: carried in bazel-orfs to measure the register-file
options on ORFS's designs (OpenROAD #11723); retires at a bump onto an
ORFS that carries it.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
